        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="THsjhZts4DkSj-40fOOM-0" parent="Dcw5bSzHjM4mUuSkkdEe-2" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Design Notes:&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;The fourteen domain use cases represent the most common areas a software engineer typically needs to build a solution.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The &lt;b&gt;codemelted.rs Project&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;splits between three programming languages.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Rust&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;provides the native implementation of the 14 domain use cases. It provides a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;codemelted&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;native command to support &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Textual User Interface (TUI)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Command Line Interface (CLI)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;scripting and development. It finally provides a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;npu.wasm&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;TAURI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;bindings to support the JavaScript modules.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;JavaScript&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;provides a series of ES6 modules implementing the domain use cases wrapping the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Web Browser API &lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;as the Browser runtime is the primary target. This provides for web site development along with Progressive Web App (PWA) development separate from this project. The WASM binding provides all the mathematical calculations made from a web target build. The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;TAURI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;binding support native Rust Desktop / Mobile app development. The modules fully support &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;TypeScript&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;and can also be utilized in the Bun / Deno / Node / Worker JavaScript runtimes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;PowerShell&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;provides the &lt;b&gt;Invoke-CodeMeltedCLI&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;that wraps the &lt;b&gt;codemelted&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;native command to have full scripting capabilities to build CLI / TUI solutions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The &lt;b&gt;rs.codemelted.com&lt;/b&gt; site provides access to each of the language SDK documentation and how they implemented the &lt;b&gt;codemelted.rs Project Developer Guide&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;Object Oriented Analysis and Design (OOAD)&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;of the domain use cases.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="290" width="816.92" x="11" y="770" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
